# lit-legs.ps1 -Describe (plan 5.17.6, M24) prints every leg as JSON
# ({"version": 1, "script": "lit-legs.ps1", "legs": [...]}) and runs
# nothing; -Leg <name> -Run <k>[,<k>...] runs only the listed runs of a leg.
# Against a stand-in build whose llvm-lit records its arguments and response
# file (Inputs/ci-legs.py), Inputs/legs-check.py checks:
# (1) the output is JSON alone, no lit ran, and every leg and run has 5.17.6's
# shape: the derived fields (pipeline, prog_pipeline, triple, runner,
# also_run) and msil_require_verify, _exec, _link and _hosted=1 on every lit
# run; the M24 rows: net-core (with $checkMsil, no native oracle, no
# msil_also_run), p3-full, harness, wsl-p3 (two runs), scale, ctest-wsl, and
# the changed wsl-net10, lto, lto-wsl, expected, expected-linux and ctest.
# $p3Tests is what 'check-matrix.py --p3-tests' prints (M24.o's
# strict-i128.c): p3-full and wsl-p3's run 1 carry every one of those paths,
# and the --filter-out of net-core and of wsl-p3's run 2 ($p3Out) matches
# exactly those tests' full lit names, metacharacters escaped. The M26 rows
# (plan 5.17.6): $checkMsil (net8 and net-core) holds
# clang/test/Sema/msil-long-double-format.c and
# llvm/test/Transforms/ExpandVariadics/msil-abi.ll; the hosted programs are
# the directories of msil/test/Programs/{zlib-full,lua,sqlite} that exist
# (zlib-full from M26); programs-hosted and programs-hosted-wsl (Quick) run
# exactly them under obj at -O2 with msil_also_run=10+tc0 (Windows: .NET
# 10, the Framework, native oracle required; WSL: .NET 10 with E7h);
# programs and programs-lto run the nine programs and the hosted ones with
# msil_also_run=10,10+tc0, programs-wsl and programs-lto-wsl with 8,10+tc0
# and E7h; det and det-wsl run msil/test/Programs/det, which holds each
# hosted program's det test, det-wsl with msil_glibc_sysroot; ctest,
# ctest-wsl and ctest-lto run the whole c-testsuite directory, unfiltered,
# with both of its lists, and ctest-lto (tag Exit) runs it under lto on
# .NET 10 against the native oracle, prog_pipeline lto. (2) What -Describe
# shows is what the runs pass: -Leg net-core, p3-full, wsl-p3, and (M26)
# programs-hosted, programs-hosted-wsl and ctest-lto pass exactly the
# paths, params and lit arguments of their runs, and -Run 2 runs wsl-p3's
# second run alone, in a row named 'wsl-p3 (run 2)'.
# (3) -Leg wsl-p3 -Run 3, -Run without exactly one -Leg, and -Run 0 are usage
# errors that run nothing. (4) The corpus parameters print as the environment
# resolves them, and the NuGet tools as @nuget:<rid>/<tool>. (5) The failure
# path of Inputs/legs-check.py: each planted fault (a $p3Tests path missing
# from wsl-p3's run 1, wsl-p3's run 2 without $p3Out, a lit run without
# msil_require_hosted=1, an lto run whose prog_pipeline is obj) is reported;
# and so is each M26 fault: programs-lto without its hosted program,
# ctest-lto without its tag Exit, $checkMsil without msil-abi.ll,
# programs-wsl's msil_also_run without 10+tc0, ctest filtering out
# libc.txt's tests, programs-hosted without msil_opt_levels=O2, and det-wsl
# without msil_glibc_sysroot. The P-1a rows (plan 5.18.10 PX4, PX5): the
# legs tagged Portable are exactly portable-smoke and portable-smoke-wsl,
# each one lit run of msil/test/Portable with exactly the params of PX4
# (portable-smoke: obj, .NET 10, 10+tc0, the Framework,
# msil_require_portable=1 and msil_require_x86=1; portable-smoke-wsl: the WSL
# runner with the portable triple, the private dotnet, obj, 10+tc0 and
# msil_require_portable=1), no other leg passes the portable triple or names
# msil/test/Portable, net-core's --filter-out matches the portable tests,
# and $checkMsil holds init-msil-portable.c and msil-dotnet.c; each P-1a
# fault is reported: portable-smoke untagged, or tagged Exit, or without
# msil_require_portable or msil_require_x86, portable-smoke-wsl with
# msil_run_netfx=1, $checkMsil without init-msil-portable.c, and net-core's
# --filter-out without msil/test/Portable.
# (6) The P-1b setup (plan 5.18.10, P-1b.c): each Portable leg's setup runs
# 'build-builtins.py --build-dir <build> --triple msil64-unknown-dotnet' and
# then 'build-libc.py --build-dir <build>' (c.dll, the empty libm.a and the
# headers in the portable sysroot), both through $MsilPython and logged to
# <leg>.setup.log, and only then the leg's lit run; -Describe shows neither
# step (its legs keep exactly name, tag, kind and runs). With the stand-in
# Python of Inputs/ci-legs.py (MSIL_FAKE_BUILTINS and MSIL_FAKE_LIBC):
# both stand-ins 'ok' make -Leg portable-smoke and -Leg portable-smoke-wsl
# PASS rows whose calls come in that order, each with the leg's build
# directory, and whose one lit invocation passes exactly what -Describe
# shows. The failure paths: build-libc.py failing (planted: exit 1; the real
# script on the stand-in build, which has no clang: exit 2, writing nothing
# under the build) makes the row 'setup failed: build-libc.py (exit N;
# <setup log>)' with no lit run, and the setup log keeps build-builtins.py's
# output before build-libc.py's; build-builtins.py failing stops the setup
# before build-libc.py runs; and the order check rejects synthetic calls in
# another order or without the build directory.
# describe-sh.test checks lit-legs.sh --describe.
# REQUIRES: msil-ci-pwsh

# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/ci-legs.py setup %t/build

